<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The activities you learned in a prior lesson taught you the properties of exponents. These same properties work with rational exponents.</para>
<para>Simplify each expression, and then check your answers. Double click on mathematical expressions/equations to enlarge.</para>
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> \({(x^2)}^\frac13\) </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^\frac23\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> \(x^\frac23\;\cdot\;x^\frac23\) </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^\frac43\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> \({(x^{-3})}^\frac25\) </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^{-\frac65}\;=\;\frac1{x^{\frac65}}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para> \({(x^\frac13)}^{-1}\) </para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>\(x^{-\frac13}\;=\;\frac1{x^{\frac13}}\)</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
</content>
